      <guid>http://localhost:1313/medical-scanner/</guid>
      <description>&lt;figure class=&#34;responsive-image&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;img &#xA;      src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/images/medical-scanner/Gemini_Generated_Hero_Image_hu_d85031371c03cbe6.webp&#34;&#xA;      srcset=&#34;http://localhost:1313/images/medical-scanner/Gemini_Generated_Hero_Image_hu_735743d6667c7051.webp 320w, http://localhost:1313/images/medical-scanner/Gemini_Generated_Hero_Image_hu_d93563cb7a550433.webp 480w, http://localhost:1313/images/medical-scanner/Gemini_Generated_Hero_Image_hu_ebdc7d462047347c.webp 768w, http://localhost:1313/images/medical-scanner/Gemini_Generated_Hero_Image_hu_d85031371c03cbe6.webp 1024w, http://localhost:1313/images/medical-scanner/Gemini_Generated_Hero_Image_hu_fb8a82b5ed5dbd40.webp 1366w, http://localhost:1313/images/medical-scanner/Gemini_Generated_Hero_Image_hu_f31fe4e133c296f2.webp 1536w, http://localhost:1313/images/medical-scanner/Gemini_Generated_Hero_Image_hu_23654be70d3174bb.webp 1920w, http://localhost:1313/images/medical-scanner/Gemini_Generated_Hero_Image_hu_47099bec758d2576.webp 2560w, http://localhost:1313/images/medical-scanner/Gemini_Generated_Hero_Image_hu_f7a8c83a1b4f6178.webp 3840w&#34;&#xA;      sizes=&#34;100vw&#34;&#xA;      width=&#34;100%&#34;&#xA;      style=&#34;max-width: 100%; height: auto; background-size: cover; background-image: url(data:image/webp;base64,UklGRpIBAABXRUJQVlA4IIYBAADQCACdASoqABgAPsVAlkUjoaEarAYAOwxE9gBOnKCprxCEP7AVyvnjvQBeuqNuWwUEPtGj4X9m7SCCzQh4DOmkVv1CXNSkfmFDi2osoFPwAP6znnqSvv7hUB2Iq4sXqkWdcIzDXePxg1gOoUBkVNDf82S9CyfXDnrXFVy5Kp&amp;#43;1mF0c&amp;#43;gH&amp;#43;8LmAb2/sc3QxX8W8R1OJkQeQQhFyoxTiprJdDc1u7E/ooYAEeEcQ&amp;#43;4xp7CPRqe/sk&amp;#43;9lVCcarLypq0ebPDc2VOpv/6S3L5kLQrbmaYe9ERkZxW4kkPWXaSHvGfAwgHijDXTq6NXudvw4tMjCMUG/zjoht&amp;#43;VbS2OtNJ9NLZUzML8NA6HOz2vAJN56BVNpQN0cUj9UyPqqmdo/8ElyyFYFqJCv5BTGtIkiHpU1PJO4HWg2LZe186xkb8PXIuACyWQyh4Uxd53Wobd&amp;#43;UguQPFy78ElLyNwjrtWca/m6DkuhUd8Rb9wSwKipdLGL3Bcrjzb6A9TyWB83Y2e&amp;#43;F8ZsQlAAAAA=);&#34;&#xA;      loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;      decoding=&#34;async&#34;&#xA;      alt=&#34;AI generated image of the Stark Medical Scanner&#34; /&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;  &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Let’s get this out of the way — what is “gravy blood”, and who is “Damp”?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This whole project started as an inside joke. My buddy and I would say we had gravy blood whenever we overindulged in a meal. That sluggish, heavy feeling afterward? In our lore, that’s the gravy blood kicking in.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Realtime BART Arrival Display</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/real-time-bart-display/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 09 Nov 2025 08:03:55 -0700</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/real-time-bart-display/</guid>
      <description>&lt;figure class=&#34;responsive-image&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;img &#xA;      src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/images/real-time-bart-display/hero_hu_5437165c78e81629.webp&#34;&#xA;      srcset=&#34;http://localhost:1313/images/real-time-bart-display/hero_hu_384d86333cef2c5f.webp 320w, http://localhost:1313/images/real-time-bart-display/hero_hu_374ea9c597eb8080.webp 480w, http://localhost:1313/images/real-time-bart-display/hero_hu_3b7a87d9784d7720.webp 768w, http://localhost:1313/images/real-time-bart-display/hero_hu_5437165c78e81629.webp 1024w, http://localhost:1313/images/real-time-bart-display/hero_hu_e8af07cb6b8db4b2.webp 1366w, http://localhost:1313/images/real-time-bart-display/hero_hu_5ef2b6a07839bc46.webp 1536w, http://localhost:1313/images/real-time-bart-display/hero_hu_570e686afe88de15.webp 1920w, http://localhost:1313/images/real-time-bart-display/hero_hu_4ede7083b909d837.webp 2560w, http://localhost:1313/images/real-time-bart-display/hero_hu_fd14a829b2d2aec3.webp 3840w&#34;&#xA;      sizes=&#34;100vw&#34;&#xA;      width=&#34;100%&#34;&#xA;      style=&#34;max-width: 100%; height: auto; background-size: cover; background-image: url(data:image/webp;base64,UklGRoYAAABXRUJQVlA4IHoAAADwBACdASoqABoAPs1Mm0YjoiEYDVVUOwzE9IBkph0&amp;#43;swQUqRXXHCEMNg/eXFaeggAA/vYA55UHWY1vYfbxsBF42UESXpfwg9itQcpS7mH&amp;#43;RfsO9Y3DM&amp;#43;H8RNYNMDaT9pS7FqGCZfIfCpxI2sSo8ZLRCrgJpJ7XAecAAA==);&#34;&#xA;      loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;      decoding=&#34;async&#34;&#xA;      alt=&#34;AI generated image of the physical BART display&#34; /&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;  &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have a love-hate relationship with BART. I’m grateful for it, but let’s just say it’s not always the most reliable so it&amp;rsquo;s nice to see before hand when the train you need is due to arrive. There are plenty of projects out there that show real-time BART arrival information. This one does that too, it’s nothing groundbreaking, but I wanted to build my own version that captures the vintage BART platform sign vibe I associate with commuting between the East Bay and my job in the city.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
